Package: cc-computer-use
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34)
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/liufeicc/cc-computer-use
Description: Computer-Use MCP server - drive a Linux desktop over MCP
 Lets an AI agent operate a Linux/X11 desktop. It perceives the UI through the
 AT-SPI accessibility tree and acts with element-level operations, instead of
 the usual "take a screenshot, guess pixel coordinates, click there".
 .
 By default the agent runs on its own Xephyr virtual screen with a private
 AT-SPI bus, so your real desktop keeps working and sandboxed applications stay
 invisible to the host accessibility bus. Set CC_CU_DISPLAY_MODE=real to drive
 the actual desktop instead.
 .
 Everything it needs at runtime is bundled - xdotool, Xephyr, xclip, wmctrl,
 xrandr, i3, dbus-daemon, at-spi2-registryd, tesseract, the OCR language data
 and the Atspi typelib - so no network or apt access is required on the target
 machine. The only dependency is a glibc-based desktop system (the bundle uses
 no host library that every Ubuntu 22.04+ desktop does not already have).
 .
 After installing, run "cc-computer-use-setup" as your normal user (not root):
 it enables the GNOME accessibility switch and registers the server in Claude
 Code if that is installed. "cc-computer-use-doctor" then verifies everything.
